# Method, evidence and provenance for {{ f.id }}

## Method

- Statistic: Welch's two-sample t, $t = (\bar{x}_B - \bar{x}_A) / \sqrt{s_A^2/n_A + s_B^2/n_B}$, with the absolute value for a two-sided test.
- Null: exchangeability of the group labels {{ facts.group_a|code }} and {{ facts.group_b|code }} in column {{ facts.env_column|code }}. Labels are permuted; the studentized statistic keeps the test asymptotically valid under unequal variances (Chung & Romano, 2013).
- p-values: sequential Monte Carlo stopping (Besag & Clifford, 1991) with h = {{ facts.permutation_h }} and at most {{ facts.permutation_max - 1 }} permutations.
- Intervals: {{ effect.ci_method }} bootstrap (Efron, 1987), resampling within each group, {{ facts.bootstrap_resamples }} resamples.
- Multiplicity: Benjamini-Hochberg within the analyzer's exploration family and across all confirmation tests of the run (Benjamini & Hochberg, 1995).

